# Security (Spring Boot)

## Secrets

- Never in code or repo; use env vars, Spring Cloud Config, or secret manager; different per environment; rotate regularly.

## HTTPS

- Enforce HTTPS in production; redirect HTTP to HTTPS or HSTS; secure cookies (Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite).

## Headers

- Use SecurityHeaders (or Helmet-like) via Spring Security or filter: X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, CSP, etc.
- Configure in SecurityFilterChain or dedicated filter.

## CORS

- Configure allowed origins, methods, headers; do not use * with credentials; restrict to known frontends.

## Input & Validation

- Validate at boundary (Bean Validation); sanitize where needed; parameterized queries (JPA); see input-sanitization.mdc.
- Do not log secrets or full tokens.

## Conventions

- Least privilege; validate input; secure headers; CORS restricted; HTTPS in prod; secrets externalized.

## Anti-Patterns

- Secrets in application.yml committed; permissive CORS; no validation; missing secure headers

